(One-edit benchmark type gate) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For the benchmark's known setup of exactly one programmed edit per clip, we tested a simple) Tj T*
(inference-time filter: the paired classifier predicts the edit type, then the localizer) Tj T*
(retains only candidate intervals of that type; if the classifier predicts no edit, it) Tj T*
(suppresses candidates. The filter threshold was chosen using five-fold passage-family) Tj T*
(grouped out-of-fold predictions on Reagan training data and a Kennedy validation guard,) Tj T*
(without loading Obama test outcomes for selection. On the held-out Obama test split,) Tj T*
(precision increased from 42.3% to 65.2% and event F1 from 49.8% to 62.7%, while recall) Tj T*
(remained 60.4%; candidate intervals fell from 137 to 89 and the 58 correctly localized edits) Tj T*
(were retained. Family-bootstrap 95% F1 interval was 50.5-73.3%. This is a useful prototype) Tj T*
(result, but the same fixed test split had already been used for earlier classifier) Tj T*
(reporting, so it is not a fresh independent benchmark. Because natural speech may contain) Tj T*
(multiple event types, this gate is benchmark-only and is not applied to user uploads.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
